# Repository end-of-line authority policy
#
# Authorized scope: MAIN_FULL81_PREFLIGHT_AUTHORIZATION_GUARD_CANDIDATE_R4,
# remediating independent-audit blocker R3-AUD-02 / R2-AUD-02 (MAJOR /
# BLOCKING): with core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes, a clean checkout
# rewrote acceptance-critical working-tree raw bytes and destroyed the
# canonical implementation identity.
#
# Candidate R3 narrowed that blocker but did not close it. Its coverage was
# maintained by hand, independently of the real raw-byte consumer set, and so
# omitted 12 historical accepted-lifecycle artifacts whose raw bytes decide
# whether a lawfully accepted lifecycle still validates. Under
# core.autocrlf=true all 12 became CRLF on a fresh checkout, their raw SHA-256
# changed, and Git still reported the working tree clean.
#
# Candidate R4 does not merely append those 12. The covered set is now the
# COMPLETE raw-byte authority consumer universe, derived mechanically from
# primary source by
# ``src.production_authority_lifecycle_u06.authority_raw_byte_consumer_universe``
# and checked against this file by
# ``src.production_authority_lifecycle_u06.eol_policy_coverage``. A bounded
# test fails closed if any future raw-byte consumer is added without a rule
# here, so coverage and consumers can no longer drift apart. The 12 paths the
# independent audit named are a strict subset of that derived universe; they
# are covered because the derivation finds them, not because they were listed
# by hand.
#
# This file is EXPLICIT and MINIMAL by design. It names only authority-critical
# paths. It deliberately declares no extension-wide or repository-wide rule, so
# no unrelated or accepted historical artifact is brought under a normalizing
# filter. In particular the seven MIXED-EOL accepted historical JSON artifacts
# under results/provenance/v7_3_to_v7_4_version_transition_candidate_r2/ are
# deliberately NOT listed and remain entirely unfiltered.
#
# core.autocrlf and core.eol are NOT changed by this policy, and this policy
# performs no renormalization of any existing object. It constrains only how
# the named paths cross the clean/smudge boundary, so a fresh checkout
# reproduces canonical raw bytes under core.autocrlf=true and =false alike.
#
# This policy is bound by the production-authority bundle under the pin label
# repository_eol_policy. It is governance/authority identity only: it is not an
# acceptance, not an audit outcome, not a freeze, and not Main Full81
# authorization.
#
# Candidate R5 (MAIN_FULL81_PREFLIGHT_AUTHORIZATION_GUARD_CANDIDATE_R5, bounded
# remediation of R4-AUD-01 only) extends this policy by exactly five
# exact-path rules, because the derived universe gained exactly five raw-byte
# consumers: the Candidate R5 checkpoint and manifest, and the three files of
# the independently audited Candidate R4 STOP preservation package. Their bytes
# are not modified. No rule is added for any future acceptance-lifecycle role
# record: those paths are not fixed yet (carried as N-R5D-04).
#
# Candidate R6 (MAIN_FULL81_PREFLIGHT_AUTHORIZATION_GUARD_CANDIDATE_R6, bounded
# remediation of R5-AUD-01 and R5-AUD-02) extends this policy by exactly six
# exact-path rules, because the derived universe gained exactly six raw-byte
# consumers: the Candidate R6 checkpoint, manifest and change ledger, and the
# three files of the Candidate R5 independent-audit STOP preservation package.
# Their bytes are not modified, and N-R5D-04 is still carried, not solved.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. This policy file itself. LF and filter-stable, so the policy cannot be
#    altered by the very conversion it governs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Canonical-CRLF authority artifacts: exact raw bytes, NO conversion in
